course: dictionary
lesson: 6618
title: Many meanings of nose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word nose can mean the part of your face you smell with, or the front of a plane, car or boat. «You smell cookies baking from the other room because tiny invisible bits of the cookies have floated through the air, up your nose» is about your face, because smelling happens in your nose.
explain: Look for clues. «Rotten eggs smell because bacteria break down proteins with sulphur in them» tells you that smell is in the air, and a nose can sense even tiny amounts of the gas that makes that smell. Your nose also warms the air you breathe in and catches dust and germs with tiny hairs and mucus.
explain: Nose can also be a verb. To nose around means to look around in a nosy way, and to nose forward means to move forward slowly. Use the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. Phrases such as runny nose, nosebleed and under your nose are common in everyday speech.
fact: The nose is the organ of smell, and it also helps you breathe.
fact: Tiny hairs and mucus inside your nose trap dust and germs.
fact: Dogs have much better noses than people, so «a dog has a good nose» means it has a strong sense of smell.
fact: When you have a cold, blow your nose into a tissue, throw the tissue away and wash your hands.
fact: Never put small things up your nose, because they can get stuck.
exercise: «You smell cookies baking from the other room.» Which part of your body does the smelling? | Your hands | *Your nose | Your ears | Your knees
exercise: Nadia says, «The boat's nose hit the rocks.» What does nose mean here? | A bad smell | The part of a face used for smelling | *The front part of a boat | To look around in a nosy way
exercise: «A dog has a good nose.» Which sense does a nose give you? | *Smell | Taste | Hearing | Sight
test: «Rotten eggs smell because bacteria break down proteins with sulphur in them.» Why can your nose notice the smell? | It is full of sugar | It makes the eggs smell louder | *It can sense tiny amounts of the gas | It can see the eggs
test: Ella says, «Jamie likes to nose around the kitchen.» What does nose around mean? | To smell a bad egg | To ring a bell | *To look around in a nosy way | To sneeze loudly
exam: What do tiny hairs and mucus in your nose do? | Make the air colder | Give you a sweet taste | *Trap dust and germs | Turn your nose into a bell
